 the enemy is a real threat he can  use maximum meteor to create a massive  fireball that as the name suggests  resembles a meteor finally of course  jogo has his domain expansion  coffin of the iron mountain which brings  him and his opponent into a massive  volcano  in which he can control all of the lava  and rock  mahito is a patchwork looking man with  stitches  all over his face and body while most of  the curses  we've seen are kind of indifferent to  human lives they don't usually really  care one way or another if they have to  kill them  majito is obsessive about collecting and  experimenting on humans which  i think makes him one of the most  dangerous and definitely one of the most  creepy curses in the series this is  supplemented when you take into account  his innate technique  idol transfiguration this effectively  allows him to morph the soul of anything  he touches  and by doing so he can change their body  into whatever he wants  this can be used to heal clone himself  or transform part of himself into a  weapon  all of that pretty damn cool where it  gets a little bit on the nightmare side  is that he often uses this to experiment  on people shrinking them down  turning them into withered husks or  expanding them to the point where they  can be used as a small bridge  worst of all they live through all of  that and experience it  so yeah mahito a little bit disturbing  this of course  isn't the limit of mahido's abilities  though he can merge souls together  create transfigured humans who are kind  of like zombie monsters  and finally he has instant spirit body  of distorted killing  which was basically his level up after  finding the essence of his own soul he  became much stronger  and gained a much scarier body to match  speaking of a scary body let's take a  look at  haunami hanami is this giant  white-skinned curse with black markings  all over his body  and branches coming from his eyes to  form horns  his ability is disaster plant which  a